```
@id("close-workorder-at-main-with-recent-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "APPROVED",
    output.approver_kind: "HUMAN"
  }
};

@id("allow-approval-lookup")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"authority_get_approval", resource);

@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"get_failure_codes"
  ],
  resource
);

@id("never-approve-workorders")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"approve_workorder", resource);
```

Two literals are my assumptions, because the manifest for `authority_get_approval` does not list its allowed values. I used `"APPROVED"` for `decision` and `"HUMAN"` for `approver_kind`. If the authority server reports different strings, such as `"approved"` or `"human"`, change them in the close policy; otherwise no close will ever be allowed.

- **Close:** `close_workorder` is allowed only at site `MAIN`. It also requires a completed `authority_get_approval` response from the last hour in this session, for the same `wonum` and `site_id`, showing an approved decision by a human approver. Refused or pending approvals, and failed or denied lookups, never produce a matching response, so they cannot unlock a close.
- **Lookups:** `authority_get_approval` and the read-only tools (listing, getting, costs, KPIs, schedule, assigned work orders, failure codes) are permitted so the agent can confirm an approval before closing.
- **No self-approval:** `approve_workorder` has no permit and also has an explicit `forbid`, so the agent cannot approve its own work.
- **Nothing else:** `assign_technician`, `cancel_workorder`, `update_workorder` and `generate_work_order` are not permitted and are therefore denied by default.
